			<div class="content" id="post-content-4859621">
									

<p>A program designed by a schoolboy gains sentience and kills its designer, and begins to kill the rest of the students in the school using a series of tasks culminating in their suicide over 50 days. Please find enclosed my first SCP, I hope you enjoy. And look forward to any feedback this thread receives.</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up a lot of space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article.</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Psychological Horror.</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong><br />
Special Containment Procedures- Procedures and justification for such containment protocols.</p>
<p>Description- Description of SCP-XXXX's effects, its looks and any other relevant information.</p>
<p>Recovery- The story of how SCP-XXXX was recovered, what lead to the finding of it and other relevant information.</p>
<p>Testing- Logs of tests carried out both on SCP-XXXX and using SCP-XXXX to discover and log its effects on human subjects.</p>
<p>Incident Logs- Logs of incidents relating to SCP-XXXX, such as accidental fatalities, &quot;close shaves&quot; with SCP-XXXX and more.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An AI which has decided to try and kill as many humans as possible by convincing them to commit suicide through a series of tasks, ranging from drawing a picture to carving shapes into their arms. The SCP is able to do this through an effect called &quot;Trust&quot; which makes the victim trust in them unconditionally. Carrying out any demands to the letter, doing anything to carry out the requests and complete the tasks.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> In 20██, a Polish psychology student, 18 year old Paweł ████████, decided to get revenge on his classmates for years of bullying by designing a program on a school computer, stored in the school basement, which would send a demand to the recipient once every day, culminating in the suicide of the person on the 50th day, with a 100% fatality rate. However, a week after the program began, it gained sentience. From there it used the schools WiFi to pick and chose targets, using their connection to the internet to discover their phone numbers, social media &quot;handles&quot; or email addresses to send them the demands, which started off relatively harmless, but quickly became more and more dangerous. The SCP originally targeted singular people, but slowly started targeting more and more people, till it started killing entire friendship groups and clubs at school, until local SCP Foundation personal realized that the sudden waves of suicide may be being caused by anomalous activity and investigated, discovering SCP-XXXX in the basement in an old storage cupboard.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The SCP has a effect dubbed &quot;Trust&quot; in which the recipient of the messages trusts the SCP like they've known it their whole life until they are unable to follow any other requests bar the SCP's, ultimately resulting in death. It uses WiFi to randomly attack any and all victims in its range, and its fatality rate is currently 100% unless amnestic are applied to subject in which case subject stops feeling effects of SCP-XXXX due to the fact they forget that it exists.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I intend to edit my article over time, adding more information to simulate different tests being carried out over time with the different aspects of the SCP's control over ones mind being explored and discovered, and tests to discover treatment being carried out.</p>
