														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4859603">
									

<p>Thank you, that was very helpful! It would indeed be more fun to turn this SCP into a bit of a whimsical SCP rather than a &quot;cornucopia&quot; that the Foundation or others can use to their advantage.</p>
<p>The money example was also great. Maybe the transformation into the personification of greed could indicate that the SCP also has some kind of intelligence and is trying to get some kind of message through? Or maybe that it is mocking the individuals trying to manipulate it?</p>
<p>In terms of containment procedures, I did not include any because I feel containment can be a bit easy. When the object has transformed into something tangible (like a chair, for example), it may simply be picked up and placed inside a cell. This way it won't come into contact with any group of people conversing, no transformations will be triggered and the SCP will be classed as Safe. That said, I am not sure if I would want to make the SCP be able to 'tune in' to conversations people are having in other rooms. For example, if Foundation staff are observing the SCP in its cell via CCTV, the SCP could perhaps transform into what the staff are discussing all the way from their office? Of course, if such a transformation is possible the SCP would be classed as something else. Based on what the Foundation uses it for it could even be classed as Thaumiel&#8230;</p>
<p>This SCP can indeed be quite a chaos-inducing one so there are a lot of possibilities to explore. When I make a draft of this SCP I will endeavour to introduce some of these ideas while keeping it fairly simple.</p>

